On Sun, Nov 10, 2013 at 9:18 AM, Wuzzy <almikes@aol.com> wrote:

> Hi!
> I want to start a little survey about how people
> learn the basic vocabulary of Lojban. I do this just out
> of curiosity, that=92s all.
>
> If you want to participate, just reply to this e-mail and
> answer these questions:
> 1) Did you learn any Lojban vocabulary so far?
>

go'i


> If you said =93no=94, the survey is done for you. If you said =93yes=94, =
go on:
> 2) How many of the gismu do you have memorized right now?
>

Around ~1100 - 1200 because the deck in Anki I used had only that amount.
I'm not sure why not all have been included and now im too lazy to start a
new more complete deck from  the beginning.

Note that I don't remember all sumti places in all those gismu.
I can't give u a quick answer on what this or that place means.
e.g. {se cusku} actually means "text" but it is even not glossed that way.

3) How many rafsi?
>

Well, {gau, ri'a, bi'o, sel,ter,vel,xel, nor, nar, tol} may be a 10 more. I
dont remember them because I dont consider them worth remembering.

I perceive {nolraitru} as an inseperable word, i.e. no different from
fu'ivla.

rafsi are good only fro mnemonic point of view. Just like fu'ivla.

4) And how many cmavo?
>

May be around 300. mekso and BAI are 2 examples of where I'm a n00b (I
remember most frequent sumtcita including {gau, bai, ri'a, sepi'o}, though)=
.


> 5) When did you start learning vocabulary?
>

When I first got acquainted with the language, probably around 2010 (at
that time I had no desire to contact the community).

6) How often (roughly) do (or did) you learn?
>

In January 2013 i made an effectively succesful attempt  to learn ~60 new
gismu every day using Anki. I never stopped until learned all of them. Now
I dropped refreshing them in my memory. There are other ways of learning
like e.g. just practicing the language.


7) On a regular basis?
>

practicing the language? probably yes.

8) Which learning tool or learning method do you use?
>

Anki for Android. There is offline Memrise for Android. I think Memrise is
fine too. It all depends on what u'd like more.

Extra question for those who already memorized all gismu, rafsi and cmavo:
> 9) When did you =93make it=94? (a rough estimate)
>

mi pu'o mo'u tadni ro le valsi


> Notes: I only talk about the _official_ gismu, cmavo and rafsi.
> Knowledge of other valsi or rafsi is not relevant to this survey.
> With =93memorized=94 I mean something like: I throw you out of bed and as=
k you
> =93Quick! What=92s the definition of =91jalge=92?=94 then you automatical=
ly,
> while still not really awake, can say the correct answer.
>

Well, once again. I know what {lo jalge} means. I'm not that sure about {lo
se jalge}. It requires me extra mental effort to translate it.

